ingle dates, amber ones are gates. Type your real dates in the table below it and they appear here as a thin bar under the planned one (green = on time, red = late, amber = in progress). The strip at the bottom shows how many workstreams run at once.</p><div class="grid" id="sum" style="margin-bottom:12px"></div><div class="card"><div id="tl"></div></div><details open class="card" style="margin-top:14px"><summary style="cursor:pointer;font-weight:600">Edit dates: planned and actual</summary><p class="l" style="font-size:13px">Planned dates are editable too (MiniMake is set to Jan - Feb 2027 and MiniMate to Mar - Jun 2027, as you planned). Each product's phases are drawn inside its window in proportion to their effort. Everything saves in this browser; use Export on the Build page to back it up.</p><table id="edit"></table><p style="margin:10px 0 0"><button id="rall">Reset all dates</button></p></details><h2>Pathways and gates, all tracks together</h2><p class="sub">Every track on one map, in time order. Arrows show what must finish before something else can start (dashed = a soft dependency). Amber pills are gates. Under each period you can see how many things you are doing at once. Compare it with the busiest months in the timeline above.</p><div class="card"><svg viewBox="0 0 1384 930" width="100%" style="display:block"><defs><marker id="ah2" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="7" refY="4" orient="auto"><path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8z" fill="#8a8882"/></marker></defs><rect x="0" y="70" width="1384" height="188" fill="#101015"/><text x="10" y="92" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#ff7a96">Business and</text><text x="10" y="106" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#ff7a96">money</text><rect x="0" y="264" width="1384" height="128" fill="#0c0c10"/><text x="10" y="286" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#ff7a96">People</text><rect x="0" y="398" width="1384" height="248" fill="#101015"/><text x="10" y="420" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#ff7a96">Techni